@startuml
title G2 - Post-quantum messaging over BLE
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam participantBorderColor #0891B2
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #ECFEFF
skinparam participantFontColor #0F172A
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam noteBorderColor #94A3B8
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #E2E8F0
skinparam sequenceDividerBorderColor #CBD5E1
hide footbox

participant "Raspberry Pi 4\nPeripheral / GATT server\nRust + BlueZ + OpenSSL" as pi
participant "Pixel 7a\nCentral / GATT client\nReact Native UI + native Rust core" as phone

== 1. Standard BLE / GATT setup ==
phone -> phone : Scan for the secure service
pi --> phone : Advertise custom service UUID
phone -> pi : Connect; negotiate ATT MTU
phone -> pi : Discover GATT service and RX / TX characteristics
pi --> phone : Service and characteristic handles
phone -> pi : Write TX CCCD: enable indications
pi --> phone : ATT write response

== 2. Authenticated post-quantum key establishment ==
phone -> pi : RX write(s): ClientHello + fresh nonce
pi --> phone : ATT write response(s)
pi -> phone : TX indication(s): PiOffer\nML-KEM-768 public key + nonce + pair authentication
phone --> pi : ATT confirmation(s)
phone -> phone : Verify pair; encapsulate shared secret
phone -> pi : RX write(s): PeerFinish\nKEM ciphertext + pair authentication + key confirmation
pi --> phone : ATT write response(s)
pi -> pi : Verify pair; decapsulate; confirm peer key
pi -> phone : TX indication: PiFinish / Pi key confirmation
phone --> pi : ATT confirmation
phone -> phone : Verify Pi key confirmation
note over pi, phone
HMAC-SHA-256 authenticates the provisioned pair.
HKDF-SHA-256 derives directional traffic keys.
Large objects use bounded application fragments.
end note

== 3. Encrypted message and visible phone proof ==
pi -> pi : AES-256-GCM encrypts "Hello, world!"
pi -> phone : TX indication(s): encrypted application record
phone --> pi : ATT confirmation(s)
phone -> phone : Reassemble; check sequence; verify tag; decrypt
note right of phone #DCFCE7
  <b>DECRYPTED & VERIFIED</b>
  Hello, world!
  React Native displays Rust-verified plaintext.
end note
note over pi, phone
ATT confirmation proves transport, not application decryption.
No application ACK or retry; Pi reports delivery=unconfirmed.
Protocol overview; physical Pixel proof remains pending.
end note
@enduml
